# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Project binaries
uuid-benchmark

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Node (testing tools)
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Never in this public repo: contains the Taurus login and internal planning
docs/plans/handoff-remote-session-recovery.md
docs/paper-context.md

# Run manifests and per-run logs. The flag dump inside them carries -ssh-user
# and the node addresses, which is the same login the two files above are kept
# out for. They belong to the paper repo's data directory, scrubbed.
*.meta.json
*.runs.jsonl
# Campaign console logs at the repo root. logs/ stays tracked: those are the
# thesis-era run logs. Without this the campaign's own log makes every
# manifest report a dirty working tree, which is the one thing that field
# exists to rule out.
/*.log
*.meta.json.*.bak
*.runs.jsonl.*.bak

# Build artifact. The orchestrator compiles the workload binary into a temp
# directory at startup; the copy in the repo root is never the one that runs.
workload

# June 2026 measurement data. Lives in the paper repo; comes back here
# curated for the artifact release, not as loose files in the root.
/cassandra_*.csv
/results-single-node-new-schema*.csv
